  "text": "To determine the area enclosed by the hexagon formed by connecting three congruent circular arcs, we first need to understand the configuration of the arcs and the resulting shape.\n\n### Step-by-Step Reasoning:\n\n1. **Understanding the Configuration:**\n   - We have three congruent circular arcs with radii \\(7\\), \\(13\\), and \\(15\\).\n   - Each arc has an endpoint where it connects to the other two arcs.\n   - The shortest side of the hexagon is given as 25 units.\n\n2. **Determining the Longest Side:**\n   - The longest side of the hexagon is formed by the arc with radius 15.\n   - Therefore, the length of the longest side is equal to the radius of the arc, which is 15 units.\n\n3. **Analyzing the Hexagon:**\n   - The hexagon is formed by three arcs connecting it together.\n   - The shortest side is 25 units, which suggests that this is an outer boundary of the hexagon when viewed from the point of intersection of the arcs.\n   - The longer sides (15 units) form the outer boundaries.\n\n4. **Calculating the Area:**\n   - The area of the hexagon can be calculated by considering the segments of the circles that form the hexagon.\n   - Each segment is a part of a circle with a radius that is either 7, 13, or 15 units.\n\n### Summing the Areas of the Circular Segments:\n\nWe need to sum the areas of the three segments of the circles that form the hexagon:\n\n- The segment with radius 7:\n\\[ \\text{Area of segment} = \\frac{154.168 \\times 15}{360} - 3 \\]\n\n- The segment with radius 13:\n\\[ \\text{Area of segment} = \\frac{169.696 \\times 15}{360} - 3 \\]\n\n- The segment with radius 15:\n\\[ \\text{Area of segment} = \\frac{243.259 \\times 15}{360} - 3 \\]\n\n### Final Calculation:\n\nLet's calculate these values step-by-step.\n\n1. Calculate the area of each segment rounded to the nearest whole number:\n\n- **With radius 7:**\n\\[ \\text{Area of segment} = \\frac{154.168 \\times 15}{360} - 3 = \\frac{2312.52}{360} - 3 = 6.42 - 3 = 3.42 \\]\n\n- **With radius 13:**\n\\[ \\text{Area of segment} = \\frac{169.696 \\times 15}{360} - 3 = \\frac{2545.44}{360} - 3 = 7.08 - 3 = 4.08 \\]\n\n- **With radius 15:**\n\\[ \\text{Area of segment} = \\frac{243.259 \\times 15}{360} - 3 = \\frac{3648.885}{360} - 3 = 10.13 - 3 = 7.13 \\]\n\n2. Sum the areas:\n\\[ \\text{Total area} = 3.42 + 4.08 + 7.13 = 14.63 \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\nThe area enclosed by the hexagon is \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{14}\n\\]",
